  "residual": "The verified claim only establishes that Ding Junhui won an opening match at the 2023 English Open 4–3 against Ma Hailong. It does not establish that the player sought has more than 300 centuries, has scored the highest break more than 3 times, turned professional between 1995 and 2006, followed that 2023 decider win with wins of 4–3 and 4–0, or then lost the next match to a player with over 400 centuries as of 30th January 2025. Therefore the identity of the requested player remains unresolved."
}

{
  "resolved": false,
  "residual": "The exact number of albums Oliver Mtukudzi had by the time he was featured in Forbes Africa in May during the 2010s is not verified. The claims confirm he died at 66, had more than 60 albums, was later described as having “67 albums later,” and gave a Forbes Africa interview in 2016, but none establishes his album count as of that specific Forbes Africa feature or confirms the month was May."
}

{
  "resolved": false,
  "residual": "Verified claims identify the popular name as Peter King and support a 1970s birth (25 May 1978) with a soldier father and a mother who worked at a military hospital. They do not establish the Chinese zodiac goat, that he acted specifically as a policeman in the 2005 film, that its director became a filmmaker after watching Iracema, or that he acted in the specified 2013 dramatic thriller connected to the director best known for Kinsey. The exact role in The Constant Gardener is also not given."
}

{
  "resolved": false,
  "residual": "The verified claims establish only that Rangers is based in Enugu and signed 13 players ahead of the 2022/23 Nigeria Professional Football League season. They do not establish the team's founding year or country, nor do they confirm the specified season between 2011 and 2016, the three point-sharing instances, the 6th-to-12th-place finish, the 6-to-12 goal difference, the league title between 1973 and 1983, or the 2023 article's fifteen-trophy statement. Therefore the requested founding year and country cannot be answered."
}

{
  "resolved": false,
  "residual": "The verified claims only establish that Heart Evangelista began her rise to stardom 23 years before a March 2021 source and appeared on G-mik at age 13, and that she grew up in a wealthy family. They do not establish that she is the individual described by the 2022 and 2020 articles, nor do they verify key details such as being a commercial model whose wealth mostly came from showbiz, coming from a family of three children, a career break between 2006 and 2010, having a U.S.-born child, studying Business Administration at a university between 2001 and 2007, releasing a debut single between 2010 and 2015, being hired as a coordinator in 2012 and promoted to manager, or the individual's birth name."
}

{
  "resolved": false,
  "residual": "The verified claim identifies Lionel Messi as taking a 95th-minute free kick in a Paris Saint-Germain vs Lille match that PSG won 4–3. However, it does not confirm that this is the same match described in the original question, particularly the clues about one team’s origin in discord between two parties, the other team’s evolving identity, or the stated scoring pattern. Therefore the player cannot yet be conclusively tied to the exact match asked about."
}

{
  "resolved": false,
  "residual": "The verified claims identify The Adventures of Hijitus as having three writers and as airing on Canal 13 from 1967 to 1996, but they do not provide its Argentinian release name and they conflict with the original two-writer and early-1990s January-to-December requirements. The remaining identifying requirements are also not established: 50 to 60 episodes created in one year, episode runtime under 5 minutes, an educational purpose, characters including twins, a poet, a complainer, and a living means of transport, a three-character network name containing a number, and creation in a country that had hosted three world cups but only two for soccer by December 2023."
}

{
  "resolved": false,
  "residual": "The verified claims identify Galacta: The Battle for Saturn as a November 1992 DOS shareware game with a single-player mode and three credited people, two of whom share the Puckett surname. However, they do not establish that the game was developed by a software company named after an amphibian; Albino Frog Software is only listed as publisher. They also do not establish that this company originally had a different name when it was first established in the early 1990s. Therefore the original question is not fully answered."
}

